WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.713
This is Allen Company training on hazard communication,

00:07.713 --> 00:11.675
HazCom for short. Under MSHA's Part 47,

00:11.675 --> 00:14.200
every mine that has hazardous chemicals has a written

00:14.200 --> 00:16.763
HazCom program. You have the right to know what

00:16.763 --> 00:18.975
chemicals are in your work area, what they can

00:18.975 --> 00:21.450
do to you, and how to protect yourself.

00:22.585 --> 00:25.272
The program has four parts. A written plan that

00:25.272 --> 00:27.497
says how the mine handles chemicals.

00:27.497 --> 00:30.434
A label on every container. A safety data sheet

00:30.434 --> 00:33.410
for every hazardous chemical, available to you

00:33.410 --> 00:36.597
on every shift. And training, like this.

00:39.910 --> 00:43.073
Every label has the same parts. The product name.

00:43.073 --> 00:46.460
A signal word: "Danger" for the more severe hazards,

00:46.460 --> 00:50.235
"Warning" for less severe. Pictograms in red diamonds.

00:50.235 --> 00:52.635
Hazard statements that say what it can do,

00:52.635 --> 00:55.048
and precautionary statements that say how to protect

00:55.048 --> 00:57.035
yourself. And who made it.

00:58.156 --> 01:01.218
Learn the pictograms. Flame: flammable.

01:01.218 --> 01:05.230
Flame over a circle: oxidizer. Exploding bomb:

01:05.230 --> 01:08.843
explosives. Gas cylinder: gas under pressure.

01:08.843 --> 01:12.906
Corrosion: burns skin and eyes. Skull and crossbones:

01:12.906 --> 01:16.481
acute toxicity. Exclamation mark: irritant.

01:16.481 --> 01:19.255
Health hazard: long-term effects like cancer or

01:19.255 --> 01:23.081
lung damage. The environment symbol may also appear.

01:24.202 --> 01:27.027
Never use a chemical from an unlabeled container.

01:27.027 --> 01:30.215
Never remove or deface a label. If you pour something

01:30.215 --> 01:32.702
into a new container that isn't used up right away

01:32.702 --> 01:35.852
by you, it gets labeled. If a label is missing

01:35.852 --> 01:38.452
or you can't read it, tell your supervisor.

01:41.780 --> 01:44.405
A safety data sheet has sixteen sections in the

01:44.405 --> 01:47.968
same order every time. The ones you'll use most:

01:47.968 --> 01:52.068
section 2, hazards; section 4, first aid;

01:52.068 --> 01:55.680
section 7, handling and storage; and section 8,

01:55.680 --> 01:57.918
exposure controls and PPE.

01:59.030 --> 02:01.930
Our safety data sheets are in the SDS library on

02:01.930 --> 02:05.005
the Allen training site, and on paper in the SDS

02:05.005 --> 02:07.630
binder in the breakroom at every site.

02:07.630 --> 02:10.830
You can ask to see any SDS at any time.

02:14.160 --> 02:17.173
At our quarries, the chemicals stored on site include

02:17.173 --> 02:20.148
diesel fuel, motor and hydraulic oils,

02:20.148 --> 02:23.648
grease, antifreeze, solvents and degreasers,

02:23.648 --> 02:27.710
welding gases, and explosives, both ANFO and emulsion,

02:27.710 --> 02:31.085
plus the rock dust itself. Diesel is flammable

02:31.085 --> 02:34.048
and irritates skin; don't wash your hands in it,

02:34.048 --> 02:35.960
and don't smoke at the fuel island.

02:35.960 --> 02:38.760
Oils cause skin irritation with long contact;

02:38.760 --> 02:42.010
wear gloves and wash up. Our limestone is very

02:42.010 --> 02:45.160
low in silica, but the dust is still an irritant

02:45.160 --> 02:48.535
to eyes and lungs. Explosives are handled only

02:48.535 --> 02:51.135
by the blaster and helpers trained for it.

02:54.466 --> 02:57.203
Allen's written HazCom program is kept in the company

02:57.203 --> 03:00.091
Dropbox, and the safety manager is responsible

03:00.091 --> 03:03.278
for it. At your site, you'll be shown the program,

03:03.278 --> 03:06.228
which chemicals are stored there, and the SDS binder

03:06.228 --> 03:09.266
in the breakroom. If a contractor or blasting service

03:09.266 --> 03:12.203
works on site, we share HazCom information with

03:12.203 --> 03:13.916
them, and they with us.

03:17.228 --> 03:19.940
Recap: you have a right to know. Read the label

03:19.940 --> 03:22.715
before you use anything. Never use an unlabeled

03:22.715 --> 03:25.665
container. Know where the safety data sheets are,

03:25.665 --> 03:29.978
and check sections 2, 4, 7 and 8. Wear the PPE

03:29.978 --> 03:32.990
the label and SDS call for. Ask when you're not

03:32.990 --> 03:33.753
sure.

03:34.886 --> 03:38.048
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

03:38.048 --> 03:39.548
override this video.
